From ad826d52d2175fc5a194c95f6d7271fe09ff6161 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 03:52:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: finish a GUI frame on the GPU before it is
 shown alone in a hold

While a change of mode waits for the video that opens (CModeChangeHold,
START), a frame of the GUI is committed alone in the mode on the screen
(FlipHeldGui(), CDRMAtomic::FlipPageAlone()). That commit has no in-fence,
and nothing waited for the GPU either: the kernel only waits for a fence
that the driver attaches to the buffer itself (implicit synchronisation),
which egl-gbm on NVIDIA may not attach. The frame could then be scanned out
before the GPU finished it.

glFinish() before the commit, as for a frame of native Dolby Vision output
that waits. The hold ends with the first frame of the video, so the cost
is a wait for the GPU on the few GUI frames at the start of a video whose
change of mode is held (HDR, Dolby Vision, a change of refresh rate).
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
index cf087cc..5073246 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
@@ -675,6 +675,11 @@ void CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::PresentRender(bool rendered, bool videoLayer)
         CEGLUtils::Log(LOGERROR, "eglSwapBuffers failed");
         throw std::runtime_error("eglSwapBuffers failed");
       }
+      // The commit of the frame alone has no in-fence (FlipPageAlone()): the kernel would wait
+      // only for a fence that the driver attaches to the buffer itself, which egl-gbm on NVIDIA
+      // may not. The GPU work of the frame, the swap included, is finished first, as it is for a
+      // frame of native Dolby Vision output that waits.
+      glFinish();
       if (FlipHeldGui())
       {
         SendDisplayReset();
